            <div xml:id="d661">

                <pb facs="0634" n="622" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg622"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.61/903: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-10-25T17:00:00-05:00">October 25, 1940—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>691. Your 1390, October 22, 5 p.m.,<anchor n="36" xml:id="d661-f1"/> and 1393,
                    October 23, 4 p.m. For your strictly confidential information, this Government
                    does not <pb facs="0635" n="623" xml:id="pg623"/> share the view that an
                    agreement, if reached, between Japan and the Soviet Union at this time would
                    “probably bring about a collapse of Chinese resistance.” You may in your
                    discretion so inform your British colleague.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
